From: <your name> <your@email>
Subject: [PATCH] Modeling Algorithms - Fix uninitialised Index read in
 Geom2dGcc_Circ2dTanCenGeo

Geom2dGcc_Circ2dTanCenGeo's constructor decides how many tangent circles to
emit with `if (Index(1) == Index(2))`, but `Index` is an
`NCollection_Array1<int>` that is never written. Trivial element types are not
value-initialised, so the comparison is `icmp eq undef, undef`, which the
optimiser folds to a compile-time constant -- and different compilers fold it
in opposite directions, so the same source silently produces either a dropped
solution or a duplicated one depending on the toolchain.

`Index` is one of four parallel two-slot arrays (`pTan`, `Index`, `theDist2`,
`theParam`) declared together; slot 1 tracks the nearest extremum of the
distance from `Pcenter` to the curve and slot 2 the farthest. Three of the four
are written inside the two `if` blocks of the extremum scan -- `Index` is the
only one that is not. Recording the extremum index in those same blocks makes
the existing condition mean what it reads as: if the nearest and the farthest
extremum are the same extremum there is one distinct tangent circle, otherwise
two.

The max accumulator is additionally seeded with -1. instead of 0. because 0. is
a reachable squared distance (the centre point lying exactly on the curve). With
the 0. seed the second `if` would never fire in that case, leaving both
`Index(2)` and `theParam(2)` unwritten while `nbsol` became 2 -- i.e. the
uninitialised read would move rather than disappear. -1. is not reachable for a
squared distance, so slot 2 is always populated whenever the scan runs (`nbext
== 0` already throws).

Observed through the public Geom2dGcc_Circ2dTanCen facade with centre point
(0, 5), which routes Line/Circle to the analytic GccAna path and every other
curve type to this one:

    curve     | clang 20 (emsdk 5.0.1) | clang 22 (emsdk 6.0.5) | expected
    ----------+------------------------+------------------------+---------
    circle    | 2 -> [4, 6]            | 2 -> [4, 6]            | 2
    ellipse   | 2 -> [4, 6]            | 1 -> [4]               | 2
    parabola  | 2 -> [2.933, 2.933]    | 1 -> [2.933]           | 1

With this change all three rows read 2 / 2 / 1 on both toolchains.

---
diff --git a/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKGeomAlgo/Geom2dGcc/Geom2dGcc_Circ2dTanCenGeo.cxx b/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKGeomAlgo/Geom2dGcc/Geom2dGcc_Circ2dTanCenGeo.cxx
index ba6939935c..8115060ac9 100644
--- a/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKGeomAlgo/Geom2dGcc/Geom2dGcc_Circ2dTanCenGeo.cxx
+++ b/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKGeomAlgo/Geom2dGcc/Geom2dGcc_Circ2dTanCenGeo.cxx
@@ -54,7 +54,9 @@ Geom2dGcc_Circ2dTanCenGeo::Geom2dGcc_Circ2dTanCenGeo(const Geom2dGcc_QCurve& Qua
   NCollection_Array1<double>   theDist2(1, 2);
   NCollection_Array1<double>   theParam(1, 2);
   theDist2(1)               = RealLast();
-  theDist2(2)               = 0.;
+  theDist2(2)               = -1.;
+  Index(1)                  = 0;
+  Index(2)                  = 0;
   int                 i     = 1;
   int                 nbsol = 0;
   gp_Dir2d            dirx(gp_Dir2d::D::X);
@@ -82,12 +84,14 @@ Geom2dGcc_Circ2dTanCenGeo::Geom2dGcc_Circ2dTanCenGeo(const Geom2dGcc_QCurve& Qua
       theDist2(1) = distmin.SquareDistance(i);
       theParam(1) = thePar;
       pTan(1)     = distmin.Point(i).Value();
+      Index(1)    = i;
     }
     if (distmin.SquareDistance(i) > theDist2(2))
     {
       theDist2(2) = distmin.SquareDistance(i);
       theParam(2) = thePar;
       pTan(2)     = distmin.Point(i).Value();
+      Index(2)    = i;
     }
     i++;
   }
